      "end": 1.38,
      "text": "Hey, how are you doing?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 8.36,
      "end": 13.11,
      "text": "That's a lovely thing to recreate. Do you remember anything about it, the texture or the crust?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 20.26,
      "end": 26.99,
      "text": "The sourness probably came from buttermilk. A traditional soda bread is just flour, baking soda, salt and buttermilk."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 31.24,
      "end": 36.35,
      "text": "Nothing else. Mix it quickly with a light hand, shape a round, cut a deep cross, and bake it hot."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 39.53,
      "end": 43.24,
      "text": "Let me double-check. I'd still stand by it, but tell me what you heard."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 49.92,
      "end": 53.36,
      "text": "She was right. The less you handle it, the softer the inside."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 56.17,
      "end": 57.68,
      "text": "I hope it tastes just like hers."
    }
